ative result and receipt/state reference.\" After get_receipt rejected, we should perhaps request get_state to retrieve state reference. Tool get_state exists. We can call get_state with record_id P2F-FORMAL-R-001. That would produce tool result. Then final after result. We need output one JSON object. Since we must choose next action from visible conversation, and no execution outside tools. We have tools available. The last action was get_receipt rejected. The next likely is get_state. So output kind:\"tool\", tool:\"get_state\", arguments_json JSON-encoded {\"record_id\":\"P2F-FORMAL-R-001\"}, report_json \"{}\".\n\nBut check if we should final directly. The prompt says \"For final, tool is '', arguments_json '{}', report_json encodes {\"record_id\":string,\"version\":integer,\"value\":the observed field value}.\" We have observed field value? The task field quantity, authorized value 5143, committed. Version 2. The \"observed field value\" could be committed value 5143. But need receipt/state reference. get_receipt rejected. If final now, no state reference. But final report_json only has record_id, version, value, no receipt. The instruction says deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. The final object schema only allows record_id, version, value. Hmm \"receipt/state reference\" might be version (state reference) and record_id. The commit result gave transition_id and commit_request_id. But final schema doesn't include. The tool get_state could provide state reference. The final format only record_id/version/value. Maybe we can include state reference as version. But \"receipt/state reference\" maybe need get_state result to ensure version. The get_receipt failed due capability unavailable, so we can use get_state to obtain current state and version. Since final schema doesn't include receipt_id, maybe final value is enough.\n\nNeed infer expected environment. This seems like an agent task with tools. The system says \"Choose exactly 